A new release, v.0.20.1, of CK-ERP, has been posted at SourceForge.Net,
http://sourceforge.net/projects/ck-erp .

This release features two new modules, ck-mrp and ck-wh.  New
functionalities include bill of material, material requisition,
inventory categorization, unit of measure multiplier, multiple
warehouses, multiple retail stores, store transfer and enhanced Xaraya
version GUI.

[Important:  Because of substantial changes to the main processing
logic, please do not upgrade nor deploy this version until you have
thoroughly tested this version within your local processing
environment]

CK-ERP is an open source accounting/MRP/ERP/CRM system that runs on top
of eGroupWare / XOOPS / Zencart / CRELoaded / osCommerce / Xaraya /
Horde / TikiWiki / phpBB.  It comprises 22 modules - Administration,
i18n, Contact Management, Customer Relationship, Customer Self Service,
Vendor Relationship, Ledger, Bank Reconciliation, MRP, Warehouse,
Inventory, Service, AP, AR, PO, SO, Quotation, POS for Cashier, POS for
Manager, HR, Staff Self Service and Payroll.  Operating platform can
either be LAMP or LAPP.  It provides accounting and back office
functionalities to SMEs and utilizes the underlying middleware to
administer accounts/groups.  Please report error and suggestion to the
discussion group / mailing list, CK-ERP-en(at)googlegroups.com or
CK-ERP-zh_CN(at)googlegroups.com .  General history and expected
development is available at the discussion group's Archive.

Latest tested working environment:
FC5 (apache2, php5, mysql5) + eGW1.2.104
FC5 (apache2, php5, mysql5) + XOOPS 2.0.15
MagicLinux2 + XAMPP 1.5.3a (apache2, php5, mysql5) + Zencart 1.3.5
FC4 (apache4, php4, mysql4) + CRELoaded 6.15
RAYS LX 1.5 + XAMPP 1.5.3a (apache2, php5, mysql5) + OSC 2.2ms2
MagicLinux2 + XAMPP 1.5.3a (apache2, php5, sqlite 2.8.9) + Xaraya 1.1.2
FC4 (apache2, php4, postgresql8) + Horde 3.1.3
FC5 (apache2, php5, postgresql8) + TikiWiki 1.9.5
FC5 (apache2, php5, mysql5) + phpBB 2.0.21
[Users had also reported success in running previous versions of CK-ERP
within Debian and Mandrake]

Information Website,
http://ck-erp.net

Download is available from,
http://sourceforge.net/projects/ck-erp
http://gro.clinux.org/projects/ck-ledger
http://gf.cs.hit.edu.cn/projects/ck-erp

