Jailkit 2.1 is released.

Jailkit is a suite to setup and deploy chroot jails and restrictive
shells. Setting up a chroot shell, a shell limited to some specific
command, or a daemon inside a chroot jail is a lot easier using these
utilities.

Jailkit 2.1 has some minor updates:
- improved logging
- allowed sub-second intervals for jk_socketd
- improved various checks in jk_jailuser
- improved handling of recursive directories in jk_cp
- new utility jk_list to list all jailed processes

For more information visit
http://olivier.sessink.nl/jailkit/

