ALM Suite rel 0.6 for SUSE EL 9 and RH EL 4 has been released by Head
West Software Inc. at http://headwestsoftware.com/products/alm_suite.html.

ALM Suite integrates multiple Open Source Development Tools into a
single installer
package for Application Lifecyle Management (we are fully buzzword 2.1
compliant) . This makes installation easy and consolidates all the tools
on a single server. Currently these tools are:

* Subversion: Revision control (http://subversion.tigris.org/
* RequestTracker: Change management (http://bestpractical.com/rt)
* CruiseControl: Integration Building and Unit Testing
(http://sourceforge.net/projects/cruisecontrol)
* Xplanner: Agile Project Management
(http://sourceforge.net/projects/xplanner)

Head West Software have an active roadmap for this OSS product and will
be adding integrations and new features over the coming months. We do
need feedback and comment from the community please -- feel welcome on
our forums and WiKi at http://headwestsoftware.com/.

Currently the ALM Suite depends on the SpikeSource
(http://spikesource.com/) application stack to run. SpikeSource is not
distributed with ALM Suite and must be downloaded separately from the
SpikeSource website (http://spikesource.com/).

Please feel to contact me with any questions.

